menu "WRO Vision"
config WRO_PARKING_MODE
    bool "Enable experimental magenta parking guidance"
    default n
    help
        Outputs visual guidance only; P4 must confirm stopping with sensors.
config WRO_LINK_TX_GPIO
    int "UART1 TX GPIO to ESP32-P4"
    range 0 48
    default 1
    help
        Binary detection-table link at 230400 baud, 8N1. Connect this TX
        to the P4 UART RX and share ground. Verify the selected GPIO is exposed
        and free on the exact camera-board revision before wiring.
config WRO_LINK_RX_GPIO
    int "UART1 RX GPIO from ESP32-P4 (-1 disables)"
    range -1 48
    default -1
    help
        When set, the P4 can retune the vision configuration over the same link
        (binary frames from vision_config_encode, or the text commands of
        vision_config_cmd.h). Leave at -1 if the link is one-way. The console
        UART always accepts the same commands.
config WRO_LINK_ON_CONSOLE_UART
    bool "Send the table on the console UART0 (USB-UART bridge to the P4)"
    default y
    help
        The camera board's USB-UART bridge (CH340) is wired to UART0. With this
        enabled the detection table goes out UART0 at WRO_LINK_BAUD, so one USB
        cable to the P4 carries the table (S3 to P4) and the configuration
        commands (P4 to S3). Logs are limited to errors so they cannot corrupt
        frames. The serial monitor must then use WRO_LINK_BAUD. Disable it to
        use UART1 on WRO_LINK_TX_GPIO as before.
config WRO_LINK_BAUD
    int "Baud rate of the console-UART link"
    range 115200 2000000
    default 921600
    depends on WRO_LINK_ON_CONSOLE_UART
config WRO_LOCK_AUTO_AFTER_FRAMES
    int "Default: freeze exposure/gain/white balance after N frames (0 = never)"
    range 0 100000
    default 0
    help
        0 keeps the sensor's automatic controls running, which is how the camera
        behaved before this option existed. The saved vision configuration
        (camera.lock_after_frames) overrides this value.
endmenu
